# Conventional Commits

- Format: `type(optional-scope): description`
- Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore`, `revert`
- Description: imperative, lowercase, no trailing period; ≤72 chars subject preferred
- Body/footer optional; breaking changes marked `BREAKING CHANGE:` in footer or `!` after type/scope
- One logical change per commit when practical
- Pairs with the `git-conventional-commit` skill (slash command is a thin pointer) for drafting messages from diffs
